   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. A few details are my own reading of the image and not certain: the L-configuration of the Asp, Lys and Cys centres, the S configuration of the lower cyanopyrrolidine, and the length of the pentyl linker.\n\n**Structural reading**\n- **Peptide backbone:** Asp\u2013Lys\u2013Asp\u2013Lys\u2013Asp\u2013Cys. The Asp1 \u03b1-amine is acylated by a succinyl linker. Asp1's side-chain carbonyl forms the amide to the \u03b1-NH of Lys2.\n- **FAP-inhibitor units (two copies):** each is a (S)-2-cyano-4,4-difluoropyrrolidine N-acylated by glycine. The glycine is amide-linked to quinoline-4-carboxamide, and the quinoline 8-NH is succinylated. One copy is attached to Asp1 through the succinyl group. The other is attached to the Lys2 side chain through a succinyl-aminomethyl-triazole.\n- **Lys2 side chain:** four CH2 groups lead to N1 of a 1,2,3-triazole. C4 of the triazole carries CH2NH\u2013succinyl\u2013quinoline.\n- **Lys4 side chain:** a free (CH2)4NH2.\n- **Asp3 and Asp5 side chains:** free COOH groups.\n- **Cys thioether:** the Cys sulfur is bonded to a succinimide ring. The succinimide nitrogen carries a pentyl chain ending in NH\u2013C(=O) on a 6-carboxy rhodamine core.\n- **Rhodamine core:** a spiro-lactone xanthene with two NH2 and two SO3H groups.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- I assigned the L-configuration to the Asp, Lys and Cys centres.\n- For the pyrrolidine C2 centre I worked out the geometry from the wedge in the upper unit and assigned S.\n- I assumed the lower unit is also S and wrote its SMILES to match.\n\n**Check on the SMILES**\nRing-closure digits and parentheses were checked for consistency and balance, and the quinoline and rhodamine substitution positions were checked against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: N#C[C@@H]1CC(F)(F)CN1C(=O)CNC(=O)c1ccnc2c(NC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCn3cc(CNC(=O)CCC(=O)Nc4cccc5c(C(=O)NCC(=O)N6CC(F)(F)C[C@H]6C#N)ccnc45)nn3)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(